<h1>Fan-out to multiple destinations</h1>
<p>In modern data architectures, a single event stream often serves multiple consumers—such as sending purchase events to Snowflake for analytics, Elasticsearch for real-time indexing, and an external webhook for partner notifications. This recipe demonstrates how to implement the fan-out pattern in Godzilla with complete fault isolation between destinations.</p>

<h2>Why fan out with independent pipelines?</h2>
<p>While you could theoretically push data through a monolithic multi-target job, Godzilla recommends creating separate <a href="/concepts-pipelines">pipelines</a> attached to a single shared source <a href="/concepts-connectors">connector</a>. This pattern provides essential architectural guarantees:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Fault isolation:</strong> An outage or slow write in one destination does not delay or block deliveries to other destinations.</li>
  <li><strong>Independent retries and DLQs:</strong> Failed deliveries to a partner webhook retry independently without impacting your data warehouse sync.</li>
